.TH UBERTOOTH\-SCAN 1 "October 2026" "Project Ubertooth" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
.PP
.BR ubertooth-scan (1) 
\- 
.BR active (Bluez) 
device scan and inquiry supported by Ubertooth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
ubertooth\-scan [\-s] [\-x]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This tool uses a normal Bluetooth dongle to perform Inquiry Scans and
Extended Inquiry scans of Bluetooth devices. It uses Ubertooth to
discover undiscoverable devices and can use BlueZ to scan for
discoverable devices.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Use Ubertooth to discover devices and perform Inquiry Scan with BlueZ:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ubertooth\-scan
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use BlueZ and Ubertooth to discover devices and perform Inquiry Scan and
Extended Inquiry Scan:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ubertooth\-scan \-s \-x
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\fC\-s\fR :
hci Scan \- use BlueZ to scan for discoverable devices
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\fC\-x\fR :
eXtended scan \- retrieve additional information about target devices
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\fC\-t <seconds>\fR :
scan Time \- length of time to sniff packets. [Default: 20s]
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\fC\-e <0\-5>\fR :
Maximum Access Code Errors (default: 2)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\fC\-b hciN\fR :
Bluetooth device (default: hci0)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\fC\-U <index|serial>\fR :
select an Ubertooth by enumeration index or serial number; see
.BR ubertooth (7),
SELECTING A DEVICE
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.PP
\fB\fCubertooth\-scan\fR takes options only. A word that is not an option, including
a bare \fB\fC\-\fR, is refused before any device is opened and named:
\fB\fCerror: unexpected argument '<word>'\fR, with exit status 1.
.PP
\fB\fC\-h\fR ends the command only once the whole command line has
parsed, so a stray word or a bad option value is reported even
alongside it.
.PP
An option value must be a whole value in its range, or it is refused the same
way instead of being read as 0, for example
\fB\fCerror: maximum access code errors must be 0\-5 (got 6)\fR\&.
